WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.468
This is JUICE:

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:05.797
one process for images and text, in
pretrained encoder spaces.

00:00:05.847 --> 00:00:09.709
Most unified models treat images and text
differently:

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.796
a language model writes the text,

00:00:11.796 --> 00:00:14.614
and an attached diffusion head draws the
image.

00:00:14.664 --> 00:00:16.374
JUICE takes another route:

00:00:16.374 --> 00:00:17.799
one process for both,

00:00:17.799 --> 00:00:19.537
learned together from scratch.

00:00:19.587 --> 00:00:22.683
Frozen encoders, with knowledge learned at
scale,

00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:25.708
turn image and text into continuous
states,

00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:28.152
each with its own noise scale and time.

00:00:28.202 --> 00:00:31.319
A flow matching Transformer, trained from
scratch,

00:00:31.319 --> 00:00:33.844
gives each modality its own projections

00:00:33.844 --> 00:00:35.451
and one joint attention.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:38.899
Time tokens tell it which inputs are clean
conditions

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:40.592
and which are being generated.

00:00:40.642 --> 00:00:43.967
Frozen decoders map them back to pixels
and words,

00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:46.254
the text in one parallel pass.

00:00:46.304 --> 00:00:48.854
Which inputs stay clean decides the task.

00:00:48.904 --> 00:00:51.904
Two times, one per modality, span a
square.

00:00:51.954 --> 00:00:54.940
Text clean, image noisy: that's
text-to-image.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:59.272
Image clean, text noisy: that's
captioning, or answering questions.

00:00:59.322 --> 00:01:01.938
Both noisy: generate them together.

00:01:02.322 --> 00:01:05.626
One model. Each task is just a path
through this square.

00:01:05.676 --> 00:01:07.227
Training covers both:

00:01:07.227 --> 00:01:10.845
conditional denoising on the edges, joint
denoising inside.

00:01:10.895 --> 00:01:13.718
Pretraining studies, one change at a time.

00:01:13.718 --> 00:01:17.036
First: should text be continuous, or
tokens?

00:01:17.086 --> 00:01:19.228
Against three token designs,

00:01:19.228 --> 00:01:22.203
JUICE leads image generation throughout
training,

00:01:22.203 --> 00:01:25.949
but its CIDEr ends just over half that of
autoregressive text.

00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:29.391
Continuous text spares images, but costs
wording.

00:01:29.441 --> 00:01:31.891
Second: which tasks should training cover?

00:01:31.941 --> 00:01:34.708
Adding joint denoising to the conditional
tasks

00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:37.450
leads on every metric, throughout
training.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.857
Train where you sample: on the edges, and
in the interior.

00:01:40.907 --> 00:01:43.522
Third: which image space to read and
write?

00:01:43.572 --> 00:01:48.357
Semantic encoders beat VAE latents and
pixels on every metric,

00:01:48.357 --> 00:01:50.682
though the VAE reconstructs better.

00:01:50.732 --> 00:01:52.940
Semantics over reconstruction.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:59.947
Scaled to 2.1B and finetuned.

00:01:59.947 --> 00:02:06.838
Visual generation: 0.88 on GenEval with
DINO, 0.87 with SigLIP2.

00:02:06.888 --> 00:02:10.412
Visual understanding, with the same
SigLIP2 weights:

00:02:10.412 --> 00:02:13.125
73.1 on VQAv2,

00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:15.578
no LLM initialization.

00:02:15.628 --> 00:02:18.885
Joint generation: from noise in both
streams,

00:02:18.885 --> 00:02:21.261
an image and a caption that describes it.

00:02:21.311 --> 00:02:22.749
Visual reasoning:

00:02:22.749 --> 00:02:25.099
in mazes with several shortest routes,

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:27.569
JUICE draws a route and writes its moves.

00:02:27.619 --> 00:02:30.717
Sampled separately, the two often
disagree.

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:33.878
Coupled, each stream sees the other at
every step,

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:36.736
so whichever settles later can adapt.

00:02:36.867 --> 00:02:39.758
Joint success, where both are valid and
match,

00:02:39.758 --> 00:02:44.433
rises from 54.6 to 93.7 percent:

00:02:44.433 --> 00:02:47.501
close to the better fixed order, without
picking one.

00:02:47.551 --> 00:02:50.701
JUICE: one model to understand, generate,

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.876
and coordinate images and text.
